<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Ablation study on key components of <span id="Sx5.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the statistics from Tab. <a href="#Sx5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Ablation Study ‣ In-depth Analysis ‣ Experiments ‣ Knowledge Graph Tokenization for Behavior-Aware Generative Next POI Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have the following observations. (1) Removing any component from <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> will cause a performance decrease, verifying the positive impact of each component. (2) <em id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o StruID</em> performs significantly worse than <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span>. This demonstrates that our StruIDs provide the backbone model with valuable information captured from the constructed KG. (3) The removal of auxiliary behavior tasks hurts <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span>’s performance, showing that learning users’ multiple behaviors is beneficial. (4) <em id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o Pref</em> and <em id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o Seq</em> suffer from an obvious drop on all datasets. This indicates that both of the user preference and the check-in history contribute to the accurate generation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx5.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
