<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Visualization of StruIDs from <span id="Sx5.F3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> and SIDs from GNPR-SID on FB dataset. Circles of the same color belong to the same region or category. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Performance on Cold-Start Scenario</h4>

<div id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">POI StruIDs preserve rich heterogeneous information, which help alleviate POI cold-start problem. To verify this, we compare the performance of <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> and GNPR-SID on cold-start POIs with fewer than 5 visitors. We choose GNPR-SID for comparison in this and the rest of experiments because it is the most competitive baseline and the most relevant method to <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span>. Results in Fig. <a href="#Sx5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Performance on Cold-Start Scenario ‣ In-depth Analysis ‣ Experiments ‣ Knowledge Graph Tokenization for Behavior-Aware Generative Next POI Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> suggest that <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> achieves substantial performance gains over GNPR-SID across all datasets, highlighting its effectiveness in handling cold-start POIs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx5.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12350v1/cold_start.png" id="Sx5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:266/99;" width="266" height="99" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Performance comparison on cold-start POIs.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Performance on Out-of-Domain Data</h4>

<div id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Generative recommendation methods benefit from the powerful generalization ability of the backbone LLMs. In this experiment, we analyze the performance of <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> on out-of-domain datasets and show the performance comparison between <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> and GNPR-SID in Tab. <a href="#Sx5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Performance on Out-of-Domain Data ‣ In-depth Analysis ‣ Experiments ‣ Knowledge Graph Tokenization for Behavior-Aware Generative Next POI Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Results from Tab. <a href="#Sx5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Performance on Out-of-Domain Data ‣ In-depth Analysis ‣ Experiments ‣ Knowledge Graph Tokenization for Behavior-Aware Generative Next POI Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> show that our approach <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> experiences a smaller performance decline on all out-of-domain datasets than GNPR-SID, suggesting a stronger generalization ability of <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span>. We attribute this superiority to our proposed StruIDs, which learn rich structure information from the constructed KG. Training with StruIDs on source data endows <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> with the ability to recommend POIs in awareness of the KG structure, e.g., recommending POIs connected by the adjacent relation. Such ability can be easily generalized to those KGs in other fields, allowing <span id="Sx5.SSx3.SSSx3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">KGTB</span> to produce better performance on out-of-domain data.</p>
</div>
